      id: 41,
      extra: `<p><b>Read the following passage and mark the letter A, B, C, or D on your answer sheet to indicate the correct answer to each of the questions.</b></p><p>The most fascinating change in societies in developing countries-and undoubtedly the most significant-is the rise of women's participation in work and education. In these nations, an increasing number of women are attending college, earning advanced degrees, and finding employment. <u><b>They</b></u> are no longer content to be housewives who only stay at home. The socioeconomic situation in these countries will be significantly impacted by this abrupt change.<br>
The financial burden placed on the male 'breadwinners' in the family will decrease as more women enter the workforce. However, they will also learn to share household duties and stop acting as the household's dominant figures and decision-makers. Children will undoubtedly benefit from this change. Their fathers will show them more love and attention. Due to the fact that both parents will be working, they will also become more independent. <br>
As a result, the service industry will face challenges first. There will be an increase in demand for after-school programs, tutoring, convenience foods, and housekeeping services. People who are more educated and have more money to spend will demand better products and higher living standards. Consequently, this will aid in the economic growth of the nations. <br><div style="text-align: right;"><i>(Adapted from https://www.futurelearn.com/)</i></div></p>`,
